---
import Base from '../components/layout/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site.js';

const endpoints = [
  {
    name: 'devices',
    hint: 'every device, with codenames, model numbers, bootloader and stock support',
  },
  { name: 'roms', hint: 'the ROMs, how they compare, and what they say works on every device' },
  {
    name: 'support',
    hint: 'which ROM supports which device, its latest build, and what works, and where each answer came from',
  },
  { name: 'features', hint: 'the features we track' },
];
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="What Android ROM Compat is, where the data comes from, how to use the API, and the licences."
  crumbs={[{ label: 'About', url: '/about/' }]}
>
  <section>
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      A list of which Android ROMs support which phones, and what works on each. It covers official
      builds only, and would rather leave a gap than guess, so anything nobody has checked shows as
      unknown.
    </p>
    <p>
      Device lists and build dates come from each ROM's own published list, refreshed every week.
      What works comes from reports, a ROM's docs for that device, or what the ROM says holds on
      every device, and each cell says which. Anything worked out rather than stated outright is
      marked inferred.
    </p>
    <p>
      A report goes stale once the ROM moves to a newer Android than it was checked on, or when
      it's over a year old.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="disclaimer">
    <h2 id="disclaimer">Before you flash anything</h2>
    <p>
      Unlocking a bootloader and installing a ROM can wipe your data, brick your phone or void its
      warranty. This site isn't an install guide. Follow the ROM's own instructions for your exact
      model, and check them first.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="api">
    <h2 id="api">API</h2>
    <p>
      The whole dataset is available as static JSON, rebuilt on every change. No key, no rate limit.
      Features missing from a support row are unknown.
    </p>
    <ul>
      {endpoints.map(({ name, hint }) => (
        <li>
          <a href={`/api/${name}.json`}>
            <code>/api/{name}.json</code>
          </a>{' '}
          - {hint}
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="licences">
    <h2 id="licences">Licences</h2>
    <p>
      The code is <a href={`${site.repo}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>MIT</a>. The data is
      <a href={`${site.repo}/blob/main/data/LICENSE`}>CC BY-SA 4.0</a>, so you can reuse it as long
      as you credit this project and share alike. ROM names and logos belong to their projects.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
